# Styling

Dark, terminal-accent UI. Tokens live on `:root` in `src/styles.scss`. Do not introduce a second palette or a CSS framework.

## Tokens

Use existing variables: `--bg-0`–`--bg-3`, `--line`, `--text-1`–`--text-3`, `--accent`, `--accent-soft`, `--accent-line`, `--accent-glow`, `--font-sans`, `--font-mono`, `--radius`.

```scss
// ❌ BAD
.card { background: #111; color: #eee; border-radius: 8px; }

// ✅ GOOD
.card {
  background: var(--bg-2);
  color: var(--text-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
}
```

## Structure

- Global resets, buttons (`.btn`), and layout primitives: `src/styles.scss`.
- Feature layout: colocated `feature.scss` with `styleUrl`.
- Shared `ui-*` components: inline `styles` in the `@Component`.
- Naming: BEM (`hero__avatar`, `panel--wide`). Kickers/labels use `--font-mono` and `--accent`.
- Respect production style budgets (`anyComponentStyle` max ~12–16kB). Prefer tokens over duplicated gradients.

## Accessibility

- Decorative icons: `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Icon-only or status dots need a text alternative or `aria-label` on the control.
- Do not rely on color alone for availability/status.
